From: Gaokun3 maintainers <zhzy0077@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: xhci: check pending descendant wakeups before bus suspend

A downstream keyboard can start remote resume between its port suspend
and root-hub suspend. The pending-resume check in xhci_bus_suspend()
currently depends on the root hub's own wakeup policy, even when the
keyboard is enabled for remote wakeup. With root-hub wakeup disabled,
the controller can be halted with the keyboard port still in Resume.

Use the USB core's count of wakeup-enabled devices for this check.
hub_suspend() collects the descendant count before the HCD suspends the
bus, and the helper also includes the root hub itself. Port connection,
disconnection and overcurrent wake events retain the root hub's policy.

Signed-off-by: Gaokun3 maintainers <zhzy0077@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 drivers/usb/host/xhci-hub.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-hub.c b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-hub.c
--- a/drivers/usb/host/xhci-hub.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/host/xhci-hub.c
@@ -1703,7 +1703,11 @@ int xhci_bus_suspend(struct usb_hcd *hcd)
 
 	spin_lock_irqsave(&xhci->lock, flags);
 
-	if (wake_enabled) {
+	/*
+	 * A child can signal wakeup with root-hub wakeup disabled. Keep the
+	 * controller running until any pending resume has been handled.
+	 */
+	if (usb_wakeup_enabled_descendants(hcd->self.root_hub)) {
 		if (bus_state->resuming_ports ||	/* USB2 */
 		    bus_state->port_remote_wakeup) {	/* USB3 */
 			spin_unlock_irqrestore(&xhci->lock, flags);
